Z||000000||lou_dias||08-10-2001||09:35 AM||||Now that my buddy offered to rebuild my blown 3.4 in my 87GT, I am thinking of some more performance tweaks.  I checked out my stock TB.  I measured the inside diameter of both ends.  The throttle body seems to be made up of 2 pieces of aluminum stuck together.<P>On the cold air side, I got 57mm, on the engine side I got 52mm.  Does this mean that I only have to bore the engine side of things to acheive the same TB offered by some people?  I'm sure I have to match the intake plenum too.  Since the butterfly is on the cold air side, a new bigger one shouldn't be necessary since that end isn't being bored.  Should I bore the whole thing to 58mm and use the stock butterfly?<P>Opinions or comments please...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||08-10-2001||10:37 AM||||When they did mine they changed to a bigger butterfly, so I guess they bored the whole thing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-10-2001||10:46 AM||||I got the bored-out TB from Darrell Morse (morse86@aol.com) and I believe he uses a different butterfly and has a custom-cut replacement gasket- as well as matching the intake plenum... $199 for the service $35 S&H.  Works great!||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou_dias||08-10-2001||12:20 PM||||That's kinda steep especially if what I mentioned is all that's involved.  you just take a razor to the gasket and it'll be matched too.<P>Anybody else?<P>1fstM6?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||08-10-2001||12:31 PM||||Here's the description of what you get for the $199:<P>Performance Throttle Body & Plenum V-6:<P>Increases intake total area by 18%.  Can you say throttle response? We machine throttle body and matching plenum to new size (57mm).  We install a new CNC'd butterfly gasket.  Throttle body cleaned and bead-blasted. Plenum sandblasted inside to remove carbon/gunk build-up. Plenum painted Fiero Red. Chrome available by request (at additional cost).<P>contact Darrell Morse (morse86@aol.com)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||08-10-2001||12:40 PM||||Actually, Darrell has reduced his price down to $125, for both the plenum and TB, and he pays for return shipping.  He sandblasts the TB also to make it look real nice.<P><BR>||||reg||14
